docs {
  # Create Project
  
  Creates a new project block for your profile. This endpoint uses the batch update system, so you can create multiple projects in a single request.
  
  ## Request Body
  
  The request uses the batch update format with a `creations` array. Each creation object contains:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `block_type` | string | ✅ | Must be `"project"` |
  | `section_name` | string | ❌ | Section name (e.g., "projects", "portfolio") |
  | `sort_order` | number | ❌ | Order within section (0 = first) |
  | `data` | object | ✅ | Project data (see below) |
  
  ### Project Data Fields
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `name` | string | ✅ | Project name (max 255 chars) |
  | `description` | string | ❌ | Project description |
  | `url` | string | ❌ | Live project URL |
  | `repository_url` | string | ❌ | Source code repository URL (e.g., GitHub, GitLab) |
  | `image_url` | string | ❌ | Project preview/image URL |
  | `start_date` | string | ❌ | Start date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format |
  | `end_date` | string | ❌ | End date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format |
  | `is_ongoing` | boolean | ❌ | Whether project is currently ongoing (default: `false`) |
  | `technologies` | array | ❌ | Array of technology/tool names used in the project |
  | `highlights` | array | ❌ | Array of project highlights/achievements |
  
  ## Example: Completed Project
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "project",
        "section_name": "projects",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "Task Management App",
          "description": "A collaborative task management application with real-time updates, drag-and-drop functionality, and team collaboration features.",
          "url": "https://taskapp.example.com",
          "repository_url": "https://github.com/username/task-app",
          "start_date": "2023-03-01",
          "end_date": "2023-08-15",
          "is_ongoing": false,
          "technologies": ["TypeScript", "React", "Node.js", "MongoDB", "Socket.io"],
          "highlights": [
            "Supports 1000+ concurrent users",
            "Real-time collaboration with WebSockets",
            "Mobile-responsive design"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Ongoing Project
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "project",
        "section_name": "projects",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "Open Source Library",
          "description": "A utility library for data processing with 500+ GitHub stars.",
          "repository_url": "https://github.com/username/data-lib",
          "start_date": "2022-01-01",
          "is_ongoing": true,
          "technologies": ["TypeScript", "Jest", "ESLint"],
          "highlights": [
            "500+ GitHub stars",
            "Used by 50+ projects",
            "Comprehensive test coverage"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Portfolio Project with Image
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "project",
        "section_name": "projects",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "Design System",
          "description": "A comprehensive design system with reusable components, documentation, and design tokens.",
          "url": "https://design.example.com",
          "repository_url": "https://github.com/username/design-system",
          "image_url": "https://design.example.com/preview.jpg",
          "start_date": "2023-09-01",
          "end_date": "2024-01-15",
          "is_ongoing": false,
          "technologies": ["React", "Storybook", "Figma", "CSS-in-JS"],
          "highlights": [
            "50+ reusable components",
            "Full accessibility compliance",
            "Used across 10+ products"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Multiple Projects
  
  You can create multiple projects in a single request:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "project",
        "section_name": "projects",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "name": "API Gateway",
          "description": "High-performance API gateway with rate limiting and authentication",
          "repository_url": "https://github.com/username/api-gateway",
          "start_date": "2023-01-01",
          "end_date": "2023-05-30",
          "is_ongoing": false,
          "technologies": ["Go", "Redis", "Docker"],
          "highlights": ["Handles 10K+ requests/second"]
        }
      },
      {
        "block_type": "project",
        "section_name": "projects",
        "sort_order": 1,
        "data": {
          "name": "Mobile App",
          "description": "Cross-platform mobile application for fitness tracking",
          "url": "https://apps.apple.com/app/fitness-tracker",
          "start_date": "2023-06-01",
          "is_ongoing": true,
          "technologies": ["React Native", "Firebase", "Redux"],
          "highlights": ["10K+ downloads", "4.8 star rating"]
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Minimal Project Entry
  
  Only `name` is required:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "project",
        "section_name": "projects",
        "data": {
          "name": "Personal Website",
          "url": "https://mywebsite.com"
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response (200 OK)
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Version updated successfully",
    "data": {
      "version": {
        "id": 8,
        "version_number": 8,
        "created_at": "2024-01-16T15:00:00Z"
      },
      "created_blocks": [104],
      "updated_blocks": [],
      "deleted_blocks": []
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  
  - Only `name` is required; all other fields are optional
  - Dates must be in `YYYY-MM-DD` format
  - If `is_ongoing` is `true`, `end_date` is not required
  - Arrays (`technologies`, `highlights`) default to empty arrays if not provided
  - `url` is for the live project, `repository_url` is for source code
  - `image_url` can be used for project previews/thumbnails
  - Each request creates a new version, preserving history
}

